    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d796">

                <pb facs="1085" n="979" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg979"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860m.00/417: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Lithuania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Norem</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kaunas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-11-16T19:00:00+01:00">November 16,
                            1939—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 17—12:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>65. Bizauskas informed me confidentially
                    that Russian troops are taking garrison positions Wednesday, Thursday,
                        Friday<anchor n="66" xml:id="d796-f1"/> of this week. President Smetona has asked Merky Mayor of Kaunas, to form
                    a new Cabinet.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Norem</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d796-f1" n="66" xml:id="d796-f1-content">
                <p>November 15–17.</p>
            </note>
